<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly steady.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly steady.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat basis bids in the High Plains were mostly steady on Thursday, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>They noted there appeared to be a bit of a glut of available supplies with some farmers starting to clear out bins to make room for fall-harvested crops.</p>
<p>Fairly active export interest was, however, seen helping to mop up some of the surplus. USDA reported slightly-stronger- than-expected weekly net export sales of 641,700 tonnes while Jordan purchased 50,000 tonnes of either U.S. hard red winter or hard red spring wheat overnight.  </p>
